246
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:55,620
he ate it.

247
00:12:55,780 --> 00:12:57,360
Yeah, it makes you wonder, doesn't it?

248
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:59,240
I should have made him my partner years ago.

249
00:12:59,580 --> 00:13:00,880
Makes him easier to control.

250
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:03,100
Oh, so that's why you're doing this?

251
00:13:03,340 --> 00:13:06,040
No! But it's not a bad byproduct.

252
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:08,140
Oh, you're kidding yourself.

253
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:09,740
You're manipulating with your checkbook.

254
00:13:09,940 --> 00:13:10,960
Maggie, come on.

255
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,760
I do not manipulate anybody.

256
00:13:13,300 --> 00:13:15,140
Mm -mm. Not with my checkbook or anything else.

257
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:20,200
So? Whoo! What do you think?

258
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:22,560
Is that the expensive one?

259
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:25,500
Extremely. Makes you look fat.

260
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:30,860
I'm taking it back.

261
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:36,180
You almost got me, Mr.

262
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:40,400
Manipulator. Maggie, I am not manipulating anyone.

263
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:42,780
If I am, may lightning strike me now.

264
00:13:46,980 --> 00:13:50,200
Ben! Um, I'm getting a drink of water.

265
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:51,900
You're sneaking in.

266
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:55,020
If I was sneaking in, would I make a mess like this?

267
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:59,440
Just when I thought you were becoming responsible and mature, Ben, that's why I went

268
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:00,320
in to bid this with you.

269
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:00,840
Need any help?

270
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:02,860
No, I can handle this myself.

271
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:05,740
Well, if you run into any trouble, here's your checkbook.

272
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:12,300
All right, Ben, what's going on?

273
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:13,920
I just wanted to show Laurel my check.

274
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:15,740
Partner? Hold it right there.

275
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:18,300
The partnership has nothing to do with this moment, Ben.

276
00:14:18,380 --> 00:14:20,120
In this room, we are father and son.

277
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:21,980
Well, then let's go back out in the hall.

278
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:25,980
What are you doing sneaking in?

279
00:14:26,380 --> 00:14:27,360
How else could I get in?

280
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:28,200
I snuck out.

281
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:30,480
Ha -ha. Ha -ha -ha.

282
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:32,660
I am so disappointed in you, Ben.

283
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:37,600
After I invested $2,000 in you, how do you think that makes me feel?

284
00:14:37,940 --> 00:14:41,760
I mean, is this the same boy that just hours ago stood in front of me and told me a

285
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:44,240
dirty joke? Hey, I got another one.

286
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:47,240
Better. Now, there's this island full of women, and they only eat corn...

287
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:48,040
Stop it right there.

288
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:49,740
Ah, you heard it, huh?

289
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:51,040
No, I haven't heard it, Ben.

290
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:53,960
The cost of that window is coming out of the $2,000.

291
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:55,260
But that's our business.

292
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:55,900
Well, never mind.

293
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,040
I told you not to bring up the business.

294
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:57,960
But you are, Dad.

295
00:14:58,340 --> 00:15:00,480
That's not fair that the money should come out of the $2,000.

296
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:01,980
That belongs to our partnership.

297
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:04,780
Oh, well, one of the partners should have thought of that before he started behaving

298
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:05,540
like a teenager.

299
00:15:05,580 --> 00:15:06,780
I am a teenager.

300
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:10,520
I'm really beginning to think this whole partnership is a mistake.

301
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:11,240
Yeah, me too.

302
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:12,640
Oh, well, there's an easy way to solve it, Ben.

303
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:13,960
The relationship's over.

304
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:16,320
You mean I'm not your son anymore?

305
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:20,920
I mean, you're not my partner anymore, Ben.

306
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:26,300
But I had such plans for us.

307
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:27,500
Come on, I had big plans.

308
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:28,460
This isn't fair.

309
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:32,580
Uh, Mom, look, would this be a good time to have a word with Dad?

310
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:36,760
Honey, you busy?

311
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:39,740
Honey, come on, I'm up to my eyeballs in this stuff.

312
00:15:40,060 --> 00:15:41,920
Okay. I'm going shopping.

313
00:15:42,180 --> 00:15:43,040
No, no, no, no, Maggie.

314
00:15:43,060 --> 00:15:44,300
No, no, sit, sit.

315
00:15:44,300 --> 00:15:45,100
I got plenty of time.

316
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,560
You know, I just wanted to see how you were doing before I left.

317
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:49,760
No, you didn't, Maggie.

318
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:54,440
You wanted a follow -up on last night and see if I had seen the error in my ways

319
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:55,540
regarding the Ben thing.

320
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:58,020
Well, Maggie, if I had error in my ways, I would have seen.

321
00:15:58,160 --> 00:15:59,080
Well, don't worry, Jason.

322
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:02,940
I won't bring up the fact that it was a mistake to mix the father -son relationship

323
00:16:02,940 --> 00:16:04,060
with the business relationship.

324
00:16:04,220 --> 00:16:05,060
I did not mix.

325
00:16:05,540 --> 00:16:09,320
Really? When you go to our accountant, he makes sure his room is clean first?

326
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:11,760
Matter of fact, I do.

327
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:13,600
That I believe.

328
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,860
Like I said, I'm not gonna bring that up.

329
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:22,300
Good. Good. And I suppose you'd change lawyers if he didn't wipe off his pork chop.

330
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:25,360
Hammond Schwartz does not eat pork.

331
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:35,160
Stop! Cricket not, cricket guy.

332
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:38,780
Oh, thanks. All right, well, how do I look?

333
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,340
Like a million bucks.

334
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:43,940
All right, well, then, the price of a new transmission should be easy.

335
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:46,180
Just one more thing, Ben.

336
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:48,060
Oh, it's not Ben.

337
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:52,280
It's Mike. Acting like Ben, dressed like Ben,

338
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:56,260
learning from his younger, taller brother.

339
00:16:57,880 --> 00:16:59,240
Leave me alone, Carol.

340
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:00,880
Don't get excited, Mike.

341
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:03,860
We're just a little concerned because you're in Ben's weenie suit.

342
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:05,240
Hey, look, this is not Ben's weenie suit.

343
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:06,200
This is my weenie suit.

344
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:10,160
Hey, you didn't sleep in that, did you?

345
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:12,040
Ah, well, why not?

346
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:12,760
It doesn't wrinkle.

347
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:18,100
Jason, your 11 o 'clock is here.

348
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:24,240
Oh, fuck. Uh, Dad, Dad, look, if you got five minutes, I'd like to show you how you

349
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:26,780
can make a lot of money with Mike Siever's acting workshop.

350
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:29,620
Out! Out, out, out, out!

351
00:17:30,520 --> 00:17:32,300
You should have told me the dirty joke.

352
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:39,380
Oh, no, I can't owe that much.

353
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:42,840
I haven't seen that many zeros since Mike was in high school.

354
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:49,000
Whoever it is, don't come in unless you got $30,000.

355
00:17:50,100 --> 00:17:51,500
I've got two cookies.

356
00:17:52,560 --> 00:17:54,540
Two cookies? All right.

357
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:56,440
What are you so upset about?

358
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:59,040
Well, let's just say I could use a couple write -offs.

359
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:01,600
I thought Mike and Ben were a couple of write -offs.

360
00:18:01,660 --> 00:18:03,180
Yeah, different kind.

361
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:05,940
It must be fun having kids.

362
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:11,980
Sometimes. I mean, when they fall for anything, like our sweet, simple Ben.

363
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:14,520
There. Ben's not as simple as he looks.

364
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:15,640
Are you kidding?

365
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:18,140
You had him believing you guys were really partners.

366
00:18:18,380 --> 00:18:19,700
We were really partners.

367
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:24,580
Sure. I liked the way you had him trusting you.

368
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:27,120
And then you crushed him like a bug.

369
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:37,680
Dad, is that you?

370
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:41,940
Yes, Dad. Hey.

371
00:18:42,260 --> 00:18:44,040
Yeah, I just got back from meeting with the Fresh Kids.

372
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:45,800
Oh, that was today, huh?

373
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:47,520
They were on that cable show I was telling you about.

374
00:18:47,700 --> 00:18:50,500
I just wanted to let them know where we stand and that our partnership is over

375
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:51,520
because I busted a window.

376
00:18:52,520 --> 00:18:56,280
Yeah. Well, uh, look, I'd like to talk, you know, man to man.

377
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:59,660
With who? Who are you, Ben?

378
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:05,340
Sit down. This will be a little difficult for me to explain, Ben, but I'm gonna give

379
00:19:05,340 --> 00:19:05,900
it a try.

380
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:08,900
See, on the one hand, um...

381
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:12,400
Ben, I'm your father.

382
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:13,880
I'm with you so far.

383
00:19:15,380 --> 00:19:16,680
Yeah, and, uh...

384
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:18,740
But on the other hand, see, I -I mean, I'm your partner.

385
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:19,860
Or at least I was your partner.

386
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:23,340
But I failed to separate those two relationships, and I should have.

387
00:19:23,480 --> 00:19:24,220
That was a mistake.

388
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:26,120
You know what I mean?

389
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:27,780
You wish to beg for my forgiveness?

390
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:29,240
No, no, not quite.

391
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:30,440
Ben, you broke the house rules.

392
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:32,080
That was your father who punished you.

393
00:19:32,540 --> 00:19:37,200
But that shouldn't have interfered with our partnership, So, uh, I made a mistake.

394
00:19:37,220 --> 00:19:41,400
I'm sorry. If you're willing to be my partner again...

395
00:19:42,360 --> 00:19:43,600
You want to be my partner again?

396
00:19:44,760 --> 00:19:46,840
Yeah. Sorry, pass.

397
00:19:49,900 --> 00:19:52,700
I couldn't just give up on the Fresh Kids because you got weird.

398
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:55,180
So I went looking for other investors and I found one.

399
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:57,600
You did? Well, that's great, Ben.

400
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:58,660
That's good for you.

401
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:00,580
Who put up the money?

402
00:20:00,740 --> 00:20:01,580
Oh, he's coming in.

403
00:20:01,820 --> 00:20:02,980
He's just parking the car.

404
00:20:04,220 --> 00:20:05,900
Uh, hey, Dad, look who's here.

405
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:10,240
Hey! Bernie, you're the partner?

406
00:20:10,620 --> 00:20:13,080
Yeah! Hey, this kid's got some head for business.

407
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:14,480
Must've got it from his mother.

408
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:16,020
Wait a second.

409
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:17,720
You're giving him $2,000?

410
00:20:18,520 --> 00:20:20,340
All right, Benny, let's see the gun.

411
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:22,640
Wait till you hear the rest.

412
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:25,180
Hey, listen, we make our deal with the Fresh Kids at rehearsal.

413
00:20:25,320 --> 00:20:27,140
Yeah, two hours later, they're taping the show.

414
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:29,300
Some guy from a record company is there, loves him.

415
00:20:29,300 --> 00:20:33,480
Ba -bing, ba -boom, they buy our contract for $50,000.

416
00:20:33,940 --> 00:20:36,940
Oh, no. $50,000?

417
00:20:37,140 --> 00:20:40,300
Yeah, and all these kids do is jump around and make noise.

418
00:20:40,320 --> 00:20:42,320
Yep. We split the profits.

419
00:20:42,320 --> 00:20:47,380
See? Paid to the order of Ben Siever, $24,000.

420
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:52,480
Oh, by the way, when you do your taxes next year, I'm no longer an accountant.

421
00:20:52,980 --> 00:20:53,800
I'm a manager.

422
00:20:54,260 --> 00:20:59,260
I ride around in limos, order room service, and I am not a married man.

423
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:04,920
Oh. $24,000.

424
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:10,880
Well, I'll be the first to admit it.

425
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:13,080
I was wrong to use that money to control Ben.

426
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:14,080
The first to admit?

427
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:15,280
And the top two.

428
00:21:16,180 --> 00:21:17,120
I was wrong.

429
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:18,380
I was pigheaded, all right?

430
00:21:18,380 --> 00:21:19,520
You happy? Very.

431
00:21:19,800 --> 00:21:23,120
What amazes me is that Ben was right about the Fresh Kids all along.

432
00:21:23,140 --> 00:21:25,320
We never should have underestimated his judgment.

433
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:27,920
We? Not we, we, me, me, me, me, me, me, me, me.

434
00:21:28,460 --> 00:21:30,100
Okay? I was wrong.

435
00:21:30,340 --> 00:21:32,540
Ben spotted their talent, and that takes talent.

436
00:21:32,940 --> 00:21:34,280
I never should have doubted him.

437
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:36,460
I'm sorry I ever doubted any of my children.

438
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:42,940
Dad, I need an operation, and the surgeon only takes cash.

439
00:21:59,800 --> 00:22:01,780
What are you doing in my bedroom?

440
00:22:01,860 --> 00:22:02,880
How about a little kiss?

441
00:22:03,320 --> 00:22:06,220
Oh, please, please, please, please, please, oh!

442
00:22:06,340 --> 00:22:09,080
Nobody makes blueberry pancakes like you do, Margaret.

443
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:10,760
Oh, those aren't blueberry pancakes.

444
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:15,160
Oh? You're sitting on his mind.

445
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:15,980
What do you think it is?

446
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:19,860
I don't really know my father well enough to guess.
